;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved
;; (all rows were fetched and byte-matched on 2026-08-22).
;;
;; FOUR independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system
;;   * the French state, via recherche-entreprises.api.gouv.fr -- the
;;     government's own company-search API over INSEE Sirene and INPI RNE data
;;     (the response carries date_mise_a_jour_insee and date_mise_a_jour_rne
;;     side by side)
;;   * Euronext, the listing venue, at its own product page for the ALSTOM
;;     ordinary share (ISIN FR0010220475, market XPAR)
;;   * the issuer itself, at its own published website www.alstom.com -- the
;;     legal-notice page this repository archives (80-data/public/tos.journal.edn
;;     archives https://www.alstom.com/legal-notice, the same URL the issuer-*
;;     rows cite)
;;
;; WHY NO COMMERCIAL-COURT REGISTER (RCS / INPI) IS CITED DIRECTLY. GLEIF names
;; RA000189 -- Sirene, operated by INSEE, the National Institute of Statistics
;; and Economic Studies -- as BOTH the register of record and the validation
;; authority for this entity (rows gleif-registered-at, gleif-validated-as),
;; and the registeredAs 389058447 is the SIREN. The per-entity pages of the two
;; company-register frontends answer 403 to this gate (see :catalog/unreachable,
;; both measured 2026-08-22). What the catalog does instead is corroborate the
;; SIREN through authorities that do answer on stable URLs: GLEIF prints
;; 389058447 three times (registeredAs, validatedAs, and inside the
;; OpenCorporates id fr\/389058447 -- rows gleif-registered-as,
;; gleif-validated-as, gleif-ocid), and the state's own API prints the same
;; SIREN with the same registered address and the same creation date (rows
;; fr-siren, fr-siege-addr, fr-created). GLEIF and the Euronext page never
;; consulted each other; the issuer's site is a fourth, self-reported voice.
;;
;; FIVE HONEST WRINKLES, SO A READER DOES NOT MISREAD THEM AS DRIFT:
;;   1. The registered legal name is "ALSTOM" alone -- GLEIF records it in
;;      French (row gleif-legal-name) and INSEE prints nom_complet ALSTOM
;;      (row fr-name). The "SA" in this repo's README ("Alstom SA") is the
;;      legal FORM, not part of the name: GLEIF's ELF code K65D and INSEE's
;;      nature_juridique 5599 both resolve to the same local label,
;;      "SA a conseil d'administration (s.a.i.)" (rows gleif-legal-form,
;;      gleif-elf-name, fr-legal-form). Two coding systems, one label,
;;      reached independently.
;;   2. GLEIF's creationDate "1992-10-28T23:00:00Z" (row gleif-creation-date)
;;      and INSEE's date_creation "1992-10-29" (row fr-created) are the SAME
;;      instant -- UTC rendering of Paris midnight. Not a disagreement.
;;   3. The issuer's legal-notice page names ALSTOM Holdings -- RCS Bobigny
;;      347 951 238 -- as the portal's owner (rows issuer-portal-owner,
;;      issuer-holdings-rcs). That is a DIFFERENT legal entity from the listed
;;      ALSTOM (SIREN 389058447) archived by this repository; the two share
;;      the registered address 48 rue Albert Dhalenne (rows issuer-address,
;;      gleif-legal-address, fr-siege-addr). No issuer-* row claims the portal
;;      owner is this LEI's entity -- each cites exactly what the page prints.
;;   4. The head-office establishment (SIRET 38905844700050, row
;;      fr-siege-siret) carries its own establishment-level date_creation
;;      2015-11-04 in the same response body. That is the date of the
;;      establishment, not of the company (1992-10-29). Do not misread one
;;      for the other.
;;   5. News headlines on the Euronext product page churn daily; the
;;      euronext-* rows cite only the instrument's identity (ISIN, instrument
;;      name, market name), never a headline, price, or volume.
;;
;; ROWS THAT WERE DELIBERATELY NOT RECORDED. nextRenewalDate and lastUpdateDate
;; (GLEIF) drift by design on every annual renewal; the state API's "finances"
;; block and Euronext's price/volume figures drift on their own schedules. A
;; catalog row that is expected to change is not a citation -- it is a
;; scheduled false alarm.

